{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "g2_depsink_dep",
    "description": "G2 (with deposition): SuperFast inlined + shared SuperFastDepositionSink mounted BY REF + operator_compose merge of the -k*c sink onto chemistry. 0-D, 1 s. k rates set via simulate parameters (exaggerated for a visible 1 s effect)."
  },
  "reaction_systems": {
    "SuperFast": {
      "tests": [
        {
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 360
          },
          "id": "base_defaults_multi_species_multi_time",
          "assertions": [
            {
              "expected": 39.386872008139726,
              "time": 60,
              "variable": "O3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 38.19570749487712,
              "time": 180,
              "variable": "O3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 36.499626128220804,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "O3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0196710112876177,
              "time": 60,
              "variable": "OH"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.017685270828760827,
              "time": 180,
              "variable": "OH"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.015266525098664305,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "OH",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.0005
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0000533748570740643,
              "time": 60,
              "variable": "HO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.00005474526969852731,
              "time": 180,
              "variable": "HO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.00005443235812673289,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "HO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0004715825087598686,
              "time": 60,
              "variable": "NO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.000310275193341143,
              "time": 180,
              "variable": "NO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.00014115184848922932,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "NO2",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.0005
              }
            }
          ],
          "description": "Reference run from upstream GasChem.jl defaults. Integrates 0..360 s with Rosenbrock23 and samples 4 active species at 4 times each. This test is the primary numerical-agreement gate between the serialized .esm and the upstream MTK ReactionSystem.\n\nTolerance rationale (test-level rel=1e-4): default band — absorbs Rosenbrock23 (upstream) ↔ Python ESS (lambdify cse=True) truncation over 360 s; loosened from a tighter starting point per mdl-1k5 after the Python runner exposed CSE-reorder noise on radical pathways. Per-assertion overrides: OH @360s and NO2 @360s use rel=5e-4 (5× looser) — stiff radicals near steady state at end-of-window, where step-size adaptation between Rosenbrock23 and LSODA diverges and CSE-reorder noise amplifies relative-comparison drift on small-magnitude values.",
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 0.0001
          }
        },
        {
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 360
          },
          "id": "base_defaults_radical_pool",
          "assertions": [
            {
              "expected": 0.39008430055736243,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "CH3O2",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.0005
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0006261317967660381,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "CH3OOH",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.0005
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.5116858193267704,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "CH2O",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.001
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 2.3348851834355124,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "H2O2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0006401785292033819,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "HNO3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 96.34083103377482,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "CO"
            },
            {
              "expected": 1.3062470823893288E-19,
              "time": 360,
              "variable": "ISOP",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.005
              }
            }
          ],
          "description": "Radical pool values (CH3O2, CH3OOH, CH2O, H2O2, HNO3, CO, ISOP) at t=360 s under default initial conditions. Guards against structural drift in the CH3O2 and HxOy pathways.\n\nTolerance rationale (test-level rel=1e-4): default band per mdl-1k5 (Rosenbrock23 ↔ lambdify cse=True drift). Per-assertion overrides reflect species-specific stiffness: CH3O2 / CH3OOH @360s use rel=5e-4 (5× looser, near-steady-state radicals); CH2O uses rel=1e-3 (10× looser — fractional-stoichiometry products from CH3O2+CH3O2 R16 [stoich 2.0] and ISOP+O3 R21 [stoich 0.87] compound truncation, and the multi-channel CH2O budget magnifies CSE-reorder drift); ISOP uses rel=5e-3 (50× looser — ISOP @360s has decayed to ~1.3e-19 ppb, so relative comparison amplifies LSODA truncation noise on near-numerical-zero values).",
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 0.0001
          }
        },
        {
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 0.0001
          },
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3600
          },
          "id": "high_nox_photostationary_1h",
          "assertions": [
            {
              "expected": 49.01536741710056,
              "time": 600,
              "variable": "O3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 24.451817558029266,
              "time": 3600,
              "variable": "O3",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.0005
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 4.931239117484898,
              "time": 600,
              "variable": "NO"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.050174382379650405,
              "time": 3600,
              "variable": "NO",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.002
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 5.7566861937418325,
              "time": 600,
              "variable": "NO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0971357341685795,
              "time": 3600,
              "variable": "NO2",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.002
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 9.30708032140729,
              "time": 600,
              "variable": "HNO3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 19.843998074464743,
              "time": 3600,
              "variable": "HNO3"
            }
          ],
          "description": "High-NOx photochemical-smog-ish regime: initial NO=10, NO2=10, O3=60, ISOP=0.5 ppb. Integrated 0..3600 s. Checks photostationary state of the NO/NO2/O3 triad and build-up of HNO3 via NO2+OH. Failure here indicates the NO2 photolysis / NO+O3 / HO2+NO / NO2+OH+M loop has drifted.\n\nTolerance rationale (test-level rel=1e-4): default band per mdl-1k5. Per-assertion overrides at t=3600 s reflect the photostationary turnover: O3 uses rel=5e-4 (5× looser, near-steady-state); NO and NO2 use rel=2e-3 (20× looser) — both species swing 2 orders of magnitude as O3+NO drains NO and NO2+OH+M produces HNO3, and Rosenbrock23 ↔ LSODA step-size adaptation diverges sharply across the photostationary turnover.",
          "initial_conditions": {
            "NO": 10,
            "O3": 60,
            "ISOP": 0.5,
            "NO2": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "parameter_overrides": {
            "jNO2": 0,
            "jH2COb": 0,
            "jH2COa": 0,
            "jH2O2": 0,
            "jCH3OOH": 0,
            "jO32OH": 0
          },
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1800
          },
          "id": "dark_all_photolysis_zero_30min",
          "assertions": [
            {
              "expected": 39.99959974182895,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "O3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 1.0314305852209193E-15,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "NO",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.001,
                "abs": 1E-12
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0007972805261944212,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "NO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 1.0534552593945216E-12,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "OH",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.001,
                "abs": 2E-12
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 1.748373575923495E-10,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "HO2",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.01,
                "abs": 1E-12
              }
            }
          ],
          "description": "Overnight / dark chemistry: all photolysis rates (jO32OH, jH2O2, jNO2, jH2COa, jH2COb, jCH3OOH) forced to 0. Integrated 0..1800 s. Without photolysis, OH/HO2 should relax toward zero while O3 and NO2 decay slowly. This exercises the parameter-override path and guards against runaway radical production without a radical source.\n\nTolerance rationale (test-level rel=1e-4 / abs=1e-14): default rel band; abs=1e-14 floors per-species comparisons for the active radicals that decay to near-numerical-zero in the absence of photolytic radical sources. Per-assertion overrides for radicals operate where abs is the *operative* floor (expected values are at or near abs): NO @1800s uses rel=1e-3 / abs=1e-12 (NO ≈ 1e-15 ppb, abs floor 3 orders above expected); OH uses rel=1e-3 / abs=2e-12 (OH ≈ 1e-12 ppb, abs is operative); HO2 uses rel=1e-2 / abs=1e-12 (HO2 ≈ 1.7e-10 ppb, lowest-magnitude radical and most sensitive to step-size adaptation without photolytic radical source). Without abs, rel comparison alone diverges as the radical → 0.",
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 0.0001,
            "abs": 1E-14
          }
        },
        {
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1
          },
          "id": "initial_conditions_t0",
          "assertions": [
            {
              "expected": 40,
              "time": 0,
              "variable": "O3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.000004,
              "time": 0,
              "variable": "OH"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.000004,
              "time": 0,
              "variable": "HO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0004,
              "time": 0,
              "variable": "NO"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.0004,
              "time": 0,
              "variable": "NO2"
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.000004,
              "time": 0,
              "variable": "CH3O2"
            },
