            },
            {
              "expected": 0.000004,
              "time": 0,
              "variable": "HNO3"
            }
          ],
          "description": "At t=0, the solver must return the declared defaults for every active species.\n\nTolerance rationale (test-level rel=1e-10 / abs=1e-14): initial-condition assertion at t=0 — solver must return declared species defaults exact-to-roundoff; rel=1e-10 / abs=1e-14 covers only parser → MTK/lambdify float conversion and the first solver step's identity-evaluation of initial state. Tighter than every other test in this file because no integration drift has accumulated.",
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 1E-10,
            "abs": 1E-14
          }
        },
        {
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 0.0001
          },
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1800
          },
          "id": "isoprene_chemistry_elevated",
          "assertions": [
            {
              "expected": 32.693040636972675,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "O3"
            },
            {
              "expected": 7.177659984147786E-13,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "ISOP",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.005
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 0.2950864782998828,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "CH3O2",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.002
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 1.3997835150361508,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "CH2O",
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 0.002
              }
            },
            {
              "expected": 103.48198722823378,
              "time": 1800,
              "variable": "CO"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Elevated isoprene (ISOP=5 ppb, O3=50 ppb) for 1800 s. Exercises the fractional-stoichiometry products of ISOP+O3 (0.87 CH2O + 1.86 CH3O2 + 0.06 HO2 + 0.05 CO) and of the ISOP+OH channels (two of which carry fractional product stoich).\n\nTolerance rationale (test-level rel=1e-4): default band per mdl-1k5. Per-assertion overrides reflect species behaviour: ISOP @1800s uses rel=5e-3 (50× looser — ISOP has decayed to ~7.2e-13 ppb, near numerical zero); CH3O2 and CH2O @1800s use rel=2e-3 (20× looser — both are downstream products of fractional-stoichiometry channels that compound truncation, and CH3O2 in particular has Rosenbrock23↔LSODA step-size-adaptation drift in the active-radical regime).",
          "initial_conditions": {
            "O3": 50,
            "ISOP": 5
          }
        }
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jNO2": {
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0149,
          "description": "Photolysis NO2"
        },
        "T": {
          "units": "K",
          "default": 280,
          "description": "Temperature"
        },
        "P": {
          "units": "Pa",
          "default": 101325,
          "description": "Pressure"
        },
        "jH2COb": {
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.00014,
          "description": "Photolysis CH2O (molecular channel)"
        },
